      en: "Poyang Lake in Jiangxi Province is China's largest freshwater lake and a Ramsar wetland of international importance. Its area fluctuates seasonally between 3,500 and 4,500 square kilometers. The lake is a critical stopover for migratory birds, especially the endangered Siberian crane. Hundreds of thousands of birds gather here in winter. It also supports the nearly extinct Yangtze river dolphin. The wetlands provide habitat for numerous fish species. The lake helps regulate floods on the Yangtze River.",
